  - "probe (kbs=1 kernel, one container, interleaved): evict_first vs no hint on W: 45.5/45.7/45.4/44.6/45.1/45.8/47.2/48.1/56.5 vs 51.7/52.2/51.4/52.6/53.2/55.1/56.0/57.0/63.7 us at B=5/16/32/96/128/131/192/211/256; cuBLAS TF32 addmm (no split) 52.2/50.6/48.4/50.4/51.8/55.7/55.8/56.1/56.2. The hint saves 6-9 us at every B [probe_b200]"
  - "probe (another container): the hint saved only 1.5 us at B=5 (53.5 vs 55.0), 1.7 at 128 and 6.1 at 211, and every absolute time was 7-10 us higher. Probe containers differ by up to 10 us, so compare only inside one probe [probe_b200]"
  - "precision: with TMA tensor-map type FLOAT32 the tensor core truncates to tf32 and max |err| vs fp64 is 3.6-4.2e-3, over the 2e-3 atol at the max. With CU_TENSOR_MAP_DATA_TYPE_TFLOAT32 (rounds on load) it is 1.27e-3 (B=5), 1.39 (16), 1.40 (32), 1.46 (96), 1.52-1.62 (128), 1.55 (131), 1.55 (192), 1.50-1.57 (211), 1.53 (256), all <= 1.7e-3, with 0 elements over tolerance. CUTLASS tfloat32_t maps use TFLOAT32 too, which explains r1's 1.3-1.6e-3 [probe_b200]"
  - "probe: k-blocks per stage (coupled W+emb ring) at B=5: 1x12 46.8, 2x6 44.5, 4x3 42.4 us. B=128: 1x7 48.0, 2x3 44.8, 4x1 79.0. B=211: 1x5 50.6, 2x2 63.3. Bigger stages help while at least 3 stages remain. Without the MMA (reads only): kbs1 43.5, kbs2 41.1 at B=5 [probe_b200]"
  - "probe: TMA L2 promotion NONE / 128B / 256B makes no difference (within 0.5 us) [probe_b200]"
  - "dead end: separate W ring (2-4 k-blocks per stage) and emb ring (1 k-block, own producer warp) was 13-16 us slower than the coupled ring in the same probe (B=5 68-70 vs 51-53, B=128 70-71 vs 53-55, B=211 71.6 vs 57). Cause not isolated [probe_b200]"
  - "step 1 (patching the CUTLASS sm100 mainloop with EVICT_FIRST) skipped: the hand-written kernel tested the mechanism directly, and shipping a patched copy of the 1000-line collective is fragile. M/L CUTLASS tiles are still unhinted [design]"
  - "build: tcgen05 inline PTX must be guarded with __CUDA_ARCH_FEAT_SM100_ALL, because target LOCAL adds -gencode compute_100,code=sm_100 and ptxas rejects tcgen05 there. Build of 2 CUTLASS tiles + the kernel takes 50 s [run_tests]"
  - "probe infra: /tmp persists only within one probe container. Successive probes can land on different containers (lost .so files); rebuild inside each probe. nvcc builds a non-CUTLASS .cu in about 1 s [probe_b200]"
  - "open: B=192/211 run kbs=1 because emb (Bpad x 128 B per k-block) fills shared memory. A cta_group::2 pair (M=256, each CTA holds half the N columns of emb) would halve the emb shared memory and allow 2-k-block stages. A 2-accumulator N<=512 version could take B=373-512 off CUTLASS (estimated about 50-63 us rented vs 68-81, limited by emb L2 traffic of 144 x B x 12 KB) [design]"
